    </attribute>
    <widget class="QTextEdit" name="textEdit">
     <property name="geometry">
      <rect>
       <x>10</x>
       <y>10</y>
       <width>441</width>
       <height>341</height>
      </rect>
     </property>
     <property name="readOnly">
      <bool>true</bool>
     </property>
     <property name="html">
      <string>&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC &quot;-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN&quot; &quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd&quot;&gt;
&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta name=&quot;qrichtext&quot; content=&quot;1&quot; /&gt;&lt;meta charset=&quot;utf-8&quot; /&gt;&lt;style type=&quot;text/css&quot;&gt;
p, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }
hr { height: 1px; border-width: 0; }
li.unchecked::marker { content: &quot;\2610&quot;; }
li.checked::marker { content: &quot;\2612&quot;; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body style=&quot; font-family:'Segoe UI'; font-size:9pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt;The&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;Input Raster&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt; section lets you choose the raster layer loaded in the QGIS project for analysis and select the color band to use for extracting intervals. You can define the analysis extent by selecting &amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;Full raster&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt;&amp;quot; for the entire layer or &amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;Current view&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt;&amp;quot; to limit it to the visible project area. You can also &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;customize colors&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt; for the histogram and classification intervals, making the classes visually distinct.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt;The &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;Classify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt; section provides options for raster classification methods: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;Equal Interval&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt; for evenly spaced intervals, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;Quantile&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt; for intervals based on quantiles, and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;User&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt; for manually defining intervals in an empty table. You can set the&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt; number of classes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;extract interval&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt;s, which will appear in a table ready for reclassification.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt;The &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;Output Raster&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt; section displays the save path for the reclassified raster file, lets you select the output location, and provides an option to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;load&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt; the new raster into QGIS automatically.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt;The &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;Menu&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt; includes actions to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;execute classification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt;, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;cancel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt; the session’s calculations, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;save table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt; values as CSV or TXT, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;save the histogram&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt; as an image, and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;close&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt; the plugin window.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt;The &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;Table sheet&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt; displays the defined intervals and allows you to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;enter new values&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt; for reclassification. It includes &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;raster statistics&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt; like count, mean, minimum, maximum, and standard deviation. You can also &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;import interval&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8pt;&quot;&gt; values from a CSV or TXT file, automatically filling the table with external data.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </widget>
  </widget>
  <widget class="QProgressBar" name="progressBar">
   <property name="geometry">
    <rect>
     <x>490</x>
     <y>580</y>
     <width>201</width>
     <height>20</height>
    </rect>
   </property>
   <property name="value">
    <number>0</number>
   </property>
  </widget>
 </widget>
